menu "H264 decoder"

config H264DEC
    bool "Enable the H264 software decoder"
    default n
    help
        H.264 Baseline Profile (CAVLC, I/P slice) pure C software decoder,
        ported from TinyH264. Outputs YUV420P planar frames, intended to be
        paired with the DMA2D yuv420->RGB hardware converter for display.

config H264DEC_MAX_W
    int "Maximum supported video width"
    default 240
    range 16 1920
    depends on H264DEC
    help
        Frame buffer allocation ceiling. Streams whose SPS declares a larger
        resolution are rejected at runtime.

config H264DEC_MAX_H
    int "Maximum supported video height"
    default 240
    range 16 1920
    depends on H264DEC
    help
        Frame buffer allocation ceiling. Streams whose SPS declares a larger
        resolution are rejected at runtime.

config H264DEC_MAX_REFS
    int "Maximum reference frames"
    default 3
    range 1 3
    depends on H264DEC
    help
        Compile-time upper bound of stored reference pictures. Total picture
        memory is (1 + refs) * 1.5 * W * H bytes; the active count can be
        lowered at runtime via h264_dec_set_max_refs().

config H264DEC_MAX_NAL
    int "Maximum single NAL payload size in bytes"
    default 32768
    range 4096 262144
    depends on H264DEC
    help
        Scratch buffer size for emulation-prevention stripping, must cover
        the largest NAL unit the caller feeds.

endmenu
